WEBVTT

00:04.650 --> 00:07.925
Note: This video is part of your Module 1 classroom

00:07.925 --> 00:10.800
instruction. The visit and tour of the mine,

00:10.800 --> 00:13.737
required by Part 48, is a separate,

00:13.737 --> 00:15.100
in-person step.

00:18.412 --> 00:21.200
Welcome to Dix River Stone. This video walks you

00:21.200 --> 00:23.612
through the site before your in-person tour,

00:23.612 --> 00:26.287
so you know where things are and how we work here.

00:26.287 --> 00:29.349
Dix River is an underground mine. It produces crushed

00:29.349 --> 00:33.224
stone, from base and DGA to clean stone sizes.

00:33.224 --> 00:36.062
The drawing is an illustration, not a map.

00:36.062 --> 00:38.124
Your instructor will show you the real one.

00:39.238 --> 00:41.375
Every shift starts at the tag board.

00:41.375 --> 00:43.700
At Dix River, it's in the breakroom,

00:43.700 --> 00:46.563
next to the time clock. Tag in every time you go

00:46.563 --> 00:49.600
underground, and tag out every time you come out.

00:49.600 --> 00:52.500
That's how we know who's underground in an emergency.

00:52.500 --> 00:55.050
Never tag in or out for anyone else.

00:58.401 --> 01:00.526
Here's how traffic moves on this site.

01:00.526 --> 01:03.039
Haul trucks run between the underground mine and

01:03.039 --> 01:05.864
the plant; road trucks come through the scale.

01:05.864 --> 01:08.201
Pedestrians stay on the marked walkways,

01:08.201 --> 01:10.888
and nobody walks on a haul road. The speed limit

01:10.888 --> 01:13.739
is 15 miles per hour everywhere on site.

01:13.739 --> 01:16.076
Traffic is two-way and keeps right,

01:16.076 --> 01:18.001
and haul trucks have the right of way.

01:18.001 --> 01:20.576
In a pickup, call the haul truck on the radio before

01:20.576 --> 01:23.201
you approach it. Watch for overhead power lines

01:23.201 --> 01:25.701
on the surface. Your instructor will show you the

01:25.701 --> 01:28.951
actual haul routes. Remember: make contact with

01:28.951 --> 01:31.939
an operator and get an answer back before you approach

01:31.939 --> 01:33.038
any equipment.

01:34.154 --> 01:37.716
We communicate by radio. The CB and the scale house

01:37.716 --> 01:40.567
are on channel 16; your supervisor will give you

01:40.567 --> 01:43.642
any other channels and call words. Warning signals

01:43.642 --> 01:47.054
here include the horn and backup alarms on equipment,

01:47.054 --> 01:49.317
the plant start-up horn, and the blast warning

01:49.317 --> 01:50.129
signal.

01:53.472 --> 01:56.235
The basic cycle here is drill, blast,

01:56.235 --> 02:00.060
load, haul and crush. Drilling and blasting are

02:00.060 --> 02:03.110
done by our own Allen crew. Dix River is mined

02:03.110 --> 02:06.335
room and pillar, on Level 1 and Level 2,

02:06.335 --> 02:09.335
and the rooms here are about 30 by 40 feet.

02:09.335 --> 02:11.498
You'll see the mining method for yourself on your

02:11.498 --> 02:14.460
mine tour. Never work near a highwall or with your

02:14.460 --> 02:15.510
back to one.

02:16.651 --> 02:18.751
The plant is where you'll find crushers,

02:18.751 --> 02:21.826
screens and conveyors; stay on walkways and out

02:21.826 --> 02:24.675
of guarded areas. The conveyors here have no pull

02:24.675 --> 02:28.076
cords or emergency stops, so never reach in or

02:28.076 --> 02:30.313
work on one unless it's locked out.

02:30.313 --> 02:32.763
The shop has its own rules for lockout and hot

02:32.763 --> 02:35.313
work. The scale house is where trucks are weighed

02:35.313 --> 02:36.863
before they leave the pit.

02:40.192 --> 02:42.780
Escapeways are marked on the mine maps with green

02:42.780 --> 02:46.405
arrows. Underground, the primary escapeway is marked

02:46.405 --> 02:49.180
with white reflectors on the ribs, and the secondary

02:49.180 --> 02:52.180
with blue reflectors, along with reflective signs

02:52.180 --> 02:54.880
and arrows. Learn both routes from the level you're

02:54.880 --> 02:57.692
working on. In an emergency, go to the gathering

02:57.692 --> 02:59.467
point: the tag board.

03:00.586 --> 03:04.249
At Dix River, the escape map is posted in the breakroom

03:04.249 --> 03:06.661
and in a covered box on the side of the plant trailer

03:06.661 --> 03:10.361
on the flat. Study it before your first shift underground.

03:11.526 --> 03:14.964
For a serious injury or fire, call 911.

03:14.964 --> 03:18.601
Garrard County E911 dispatches all three.

03:18.601 --> 03:23.439
Tell them: Dix River Stone, 4963 Danville Rd,

03:23.439 --> 03:26.064
Lancaster, and where the injured person is:

03:26.064 --> 03:29.951
underground, pit, plant, scale or shop.

03:29.951 --> 03:32.163
Then call the mine office so someone meets the

03:32.163 --> 03:35.314
ambulance at the gate. Nearby hospitals are Ephraim

03:35.314 --> 03:38.913
McDowell RMC, Ephraim McDowell Fort Logan,

03:38.913 --> 03:41.464
Baptist Health Richmond. Mine rescue comes from

03:41.464 --> 03:44.138
the Kentucky Division of Mine Safety's Crestwood

03:44.138 --> 03:46.326
and Hazard mine rescue stations.

03:47.446 --> 03:49.896
Your in-person mine tour is the next,

03:49.896 --> 03:52.358
separate step. Ask questions about anything you

03:52.358 --> 03:53.096
see.

03:54.208 --> 03:57.370
Remember: your site's plans and procedures always

03:57.370 --> 03:58.871
override this video.
